# Figure and table generators

`python code/figures/render_all.py` (from the repository root; needs `numpy`, `matplotlib`) renders every figure/table into
`paper/figures/` (PDF, fonts embedded as TrueType) and `paper/tables/` (LaTeX, booktabs) from `results/` only.
`figstyle.py` holds the shared style (text width 5.5 in, Okabe-Ito colours plus distinct markers/linestyles for B/W).

Inputs are read from `results/` (override with `RESULTS_DIR=/path/to/results`); every output gets a `<name>.inputs.json` with the sha256 of the result files it was made from.
